        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION DAILY REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: 
REF HIL 107144535
DATUM AIRCRAFT EXPERIENCED 2X RH BLEED TRIP. 
ON PREVIOUS FLIGHT LEGS, ACMS DATA SHOWS RHS PRESSURE TO BE LOW  ALL STAGES OF FLIGHT. 
LOW DURING CLIMB (MAX 26 PSI, STEADY DECAY), DURING CRUISE (14 PSI).
FURTHER ACTION REQUIRED.

ACTION:  

1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.
	
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
	
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.
	
3. CHECK  DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE PN 16135-81 FOR OBSTRUCTION USING COMPRESSED NITROGEN. 

4.  LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:
    A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE
    B) SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV
    C) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR

5. CLOSELY INSPECT RH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.

6. INSPECT THE #2 PCCV KISS SEAL IAW AMM 36-12-02. REPLACE IF NECESSARY

7.  CHECK BLEED AIR REGULATOR FOR D/S PORT LEAKAGE OR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.

8. IF NFF, REPLACE THE FOLLOWING COMPONENTS:

A) THE #2 BLEED AIR REGULATOR IAW AMM 36-11-03/401.

B) THE #2 HIGH STAGE REGULATOR IAW 36-11-07/401.

9. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE WITH ALL FINDINGS FROM THIS W/O DOCUMENTED AND CLOSED EITHER THROUGH POSITIVE MAINTENANCE ACTION OR AN ACCEPTABLE DEFERRAL. 

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
